# Prepare for Deployment

Trigger phrases: **prepare for deployment**, **prep for deploy**, **deploy prep**.

When the user says any of these, run this checklist. Do not skip steps. Do not commit or push unless they explicitly ask.

## 1. Bump cache-bust hashes

From repo root (prefer Python; Node copy is optional):

```bash
python _tools/bump-asset-hashes.py
```

Fallback if Node is available: `node _tools/bump-asset-hashes.js`

- Updates root live HTML only (`index.html`, `gallery.html`, `about.html`, `contact.html`, `resume.html`, `projects2.html`, etc.).
- Sets `?v=<8-char-sha>` on `style.css`, `colorbox.css`, and `sidebar-loader.js` from file contents.
- Bumps site build id (`YYYY.MM.DD.N` in `_tools/site-version.txt`) into each HTML page: `<!-- iancw-build: … -->`, `<meta name="site-version">`, and `<body data-build="…">`.
- Use `python _tools/bump-asset-hashes.py --all` only if they ask to include `Archive/`.

## 2. Spot-check

- Confirm live pages reference `style.css?v=...` (not bare `style.css`).
- Confirm `_tools/` was not added under a public path that Pages would serve (keep tooling in `_tools/`).
- Summarize which HTML files changed and the new hashes.

## 3. Remind (do not run unless asked)

- Commit when they ask (include HTML + any CSS/JS + `_tools` if new).
- After push to GitHub Pages: Fastly may still HIT old objects for a few minutes; the new `?v=` URLs bypass that for CSS/JS.
- Cloudflare Dev Mode does not bypass GitHub Fastly; purge CF only if needed for HTML.

## 4. Out of scope for this phrase

- Do not redesign pages or refactor CSS.
- Do not amend git history or force-push.
